  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency grant for the Cambodia&#x2013;Thailand border areasEmergency grant for the Cambodia&#x2013;Thailand border areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The escalation of the Thailand&#x2013;Cambodia border conflict in May&#x2013;July 2025 has displaced over 134,000 people in Cambodia, overwhelming temporary shelters and exposing critical gaps in shelter, water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH), and protection services. Despite a ceasefire, ongoing population movements, political sensitivities, and limited coordination continue to challenge response efforts.In response, IOM Cambodia proposes a six-month emergency intervention to address the urgent humanitarian needs of displaced populations, returning migrants, and vulnerable host communities. The project is providing coordinated site management, emergency shelter, and essential non-food and hygiene items, with distribution plans designed to adapt to population movements and evolving needs. Working closely with national and local authorities, partners, and communities, IOM is ensuring timely and targeted assistance while promoting protection, dignity, and efficient resource use.</narrative>
  </description>
